@misc{Łukawski_24223,
 abstract = {Allagma is a composition presented as three short preludes for the MIDI grand piano.

Allagma is also a composition system working as a self-contained composer—a system that generates a new realisation each time it runs. It operates in two phases.

Phase 1: the system prompts a reasoning language model to design its own musical vocabulary in the Decentralised Creative Network. The agent iteratively evaluates what it has produced so far, enlarging and diversifying its vocabulary of reusable modules.

Phase 2: the system composes with that vocabulary by acting as a scheduler—deciding when and how each piece of the musical vocabulary should enter—to produce a structured piece with interleaved episodes, reprises, and silences. 

In Allagma the work exists as a system that reconfigures its operational structure to produce new versions while preserving procedural identity. My role here shifts from designing specific transformations to designing the conditions under which a vocabulary can emerge. The result is co-construction: I set boundaries and evaluation criteria; the AI agent populates the space with its own creativity.

Three contrasting realisations produced by this system were curated for the concert.
},
